rapher\">Charles J. Sharp</span></a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":81861011,"title":"File:Outside view of Wartburg Castle (4).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/99/Outside_view_of_Wartburg_Castle_%284%29.jpg/960px-Outside_view_of_Wartburg_Castle_%284%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Outside_view_of_Wartburg_Castle_(4).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Outside view of Wartburg Castle in Eisenach, Thuringia, Germany"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2018-10-09 08:50:16"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Tournasol7\" title=\"User:Tournasol7\">Krzysztof Golik</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":99860271,"title":"File:Ou-Line-Series701-N12.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Ou-Line-Series701-N12.jpg/960px-Ou-Line-Series701-N12.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ou-Line-Series701-N12.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Japan_Railway_Company\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:East Japan Railway Company\">JR East</a> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/701_series\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:701 series\">701 series</a> N12 train between Naijōshi and Kawabe on the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C5%8Cu_Main_Line\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Ōu Main Line\">Ōu Main Line</a>, Japan"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2016-12-11 10:04:37"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:MaedaAkihiko\" title=\"User:MaedaAkihiko\">MaedaAkihiko</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":123591552,"title":"File:Ovenbird (90497).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Ovenbird_%2890497%29.jpg/960px-Ovenbird_%2890497%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ovenbird_(90497).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Ovenbird in Prospect Park (Brooklyn, NY, USA)"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2022-09-29 15:54:27"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/User:Rhododendrites\" title=\"User:Rhododendrites\">Rhododendrites</a>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":128846191,"title":"File:Ourapteryx yerburii ssp. specimens and male genitalia.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Ourapteryx_yerburii_ssp._specimens_and_male_genitalia.jpg/960px-Ourapteryx_yerburii_ssp._specimens_and_male_genitalia.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ourapteryx_yerburii_ssp._specimens_and_male_genitalia.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Overview of the two known subspecies of geometrid moth <i>Ourapteryx yerburii</i>: <i>yerburii</i> and <i>virescens</i>, with mounted male specimens and genitalia (aedeagi displayed seperately) are shown. As described by Inoue, the facies and sizes of these two subspecies are almost identical, except that the furca in the male genitalia of <i>virescens</i> \"is not so acutely downcurved nor dilated\"<sup id=\"cite_ref-Inoue_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Inoue-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>.\n<p>The abdomen of <i>yerburii</i> was removed to extract the genitalia inside.\n</p>\n<ul><li><b><i>Ourapteryx yerburii yerburii</i> (Butler, 1886)</b>\n<ul><li>Mounted specimen/Genitalia slide: NHMUK 015106199\n<ul><li>Locality: Godawari at 1600 m, Lalitpur, Nepal</li>\n<li>Collected: 8.v.1991, leg. H. Inoue [<div lang=\"ja\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"description ja\" style=\"display:inline;\">井上寛</div>].</li>\n<li>Genitalia slide prepared by H. Inoue (slide no. 15076)</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>\n<ul><li><b><i>Ourapteryx yerburii virescens</i> (Matsumura, 1910)</b>\n<ul><li>Mounted specimen: NHMUK 015106200\n<ul><li>Locality: Erge-shan Trail at 523 m, Shiding, New Taipei City, Taiwan</li>\n<li>Collected: 16.v.2007, leg. G. Martin &amp; D. L. J. Quicke.</li></ul></li>\n<li>Genitalia slide: NHMUK 015106197\n<ul><li>Locality: Lalashan, New Taipei City, Taiwan</li>\n<li>Collected: 26-28.vi.1979, leg. H. Inoue.</li>\n<li>Prepared by H. Inoue (slide no. 10322)</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>"},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"2023-02-10 11:39:38"},"Artist":{"value":"<a href=\"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/User:Tiouraren\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"zh-tw:User:Tiouraren\">Tiouraren</a> (Y.-C. Tsai)"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}}}]},{"pageid":151142199,"title":"File:Oval portrait miniature of girl oil painting by Valentine Manchon Duchesne - with scale.jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/98/Oval_portrait_miniature_of_girl_oil_painting_by_Valentine_Manchon_Duchesne_-_with_scale.jpg/960px-Oval_portrait_miniature_of_girl_oil_painting_by_Valentine_Manchon_Duchesne_-_with_scale.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Oval_portrait_miniature_of_girl_oil_painting_by_Valentine_Manchon_Duchesne_-_with_scale.jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Oval <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portrait_miniature\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Portrait miniature\">portrait miniature</a> of a blond girl, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oil_painting\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Oil painting\">oil painting</a> by <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Category:Valentine_Manchon_Duchesne\" title=\"Category:Valentine Manchon Duchesne\">Valentine Manchon Duchesne</a> from France. 19th century. Dimensions: 35 x 46 mm (1.38 x 1.81 in). Signed. Oval golden metal frame. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macro_photography\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Macro photography\">Macro photography</a> from original artwork. One centimetre indicative cale added on the photo."},"DateTimeOriginal":{"value":"19<sup>th</sup> century<div style=\"display: none;\">date QS:P571,+1850-00-00T00:00:00Z/7</div>"},"Artist":{"value":"<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q126951825\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q126951825\"><span title=\"French painter\">Valentine Manchon Duchesne</span></a></bdi>"},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain"}}}]},{"pageid":153640743,"title":"File:Our Lady of Sameiro sanctuary in Braga (1).jpg","imageinfo":[{"thumburl":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Our_Lady_of_Sameiro_sanctuary_in_Braga_%281%29.jpg/960px-Our_Lady_of_Sameiro_sanctuary_in_Braga_%281%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Our_Lady_of_Sameiro_sanctuary_in_Braga_(1).jpg","extmetadata":{"ImageDescription":{"value":"Our Lady of Sameiro sanctuary in Braga, Braga District, Portugal\n<table cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"text-align:left; color:#000; background:#F2EFD0; border:1px solid #BBA22C; margin:1px;\" dir=\"ltr\" class=\"layouttemplate\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:SIPA_logo_(cropped).png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/SIPA_logo_%28cropped%29.png/60px-SIPA_logo_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"41\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/SIPA_logo_%28cropped%29.png?utm_source=commons.wiki